ns with `0.29` (gives 28 instead of 29) and `4.35` (gives 434 instead of 435), so every test that went through `Line.cents()` came out a cent short or worse.\n\n**Fix:** `to_cents` now converts the price through `Decimal(str(amount))`, which keeps the price as written, and rounds half up to a whole cent. That rounding rule matches the existing rounding in `discounts.py` and `tax.py`. The rest of the code still works in whole cents, so nothing else changed.\n\n**Possible follow-up:** prices still come in as floats (`Line(\"A1\", 19.99)`). `str()` gives back the decimal you typed for ordinary prices, but a safer long-term setup would be to accept `Decimal` or integer cents at the `Line` boundary.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 0, "replies_ok": 5, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 64198, "requests_cache_write": 14663, "requests_cost_usd": 0.12116260000000001, "requests_count": 5, "requests_input_uncached": 12, "requests_output": 1748, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-multistep:claude-opus-5-5:trial1", "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 3, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-13T04:47:23.265867+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 21.848, "t_checker_s": 0.38, "t_env_setup_s": 0.001, "task": "trig-omp-multistep", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "off", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s": 360, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "estimated", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens": 1760, "tokens_cache_read": 64198, "tokens_cache_write": 14663, "tokens_fresh": 1760, "tokens_input_uncached": 12, "tokens_main_cache_read": 64198, "tokens_main_cache_write": 14663, "tokens_main_calls": 5, "tokens_main_input_uncached": 12, "tokens_main_output": 1748, "tokens_output": 1748, "tokens_proxy_cache_read": 64198, "tokens_proxy_cache_wr