 `Decimal(str(amount))`. `str()` gives the shortest exact form of the float, so `19.99` stays `19.99`. That value is multiplied by 100 and rounded to a whole cent with `ROUND_HALF_UP`, which matches how the discount and tax code already rounds. Ints, strings and `Decimal` inputs still work.\n\nThe real issue is that `Line.unit_price` takes floats in the first place. Prices should come in as `Decimal` or integer cents from the boundary. That change affects the public API, so I didn't make it here.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 1, "replies_ok": 7, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 94484, "requests_cache_write": 17627, "requests_cost_usd": 0.14733580000000002, "requests_count": 7, "requests_input_uncached": 16, "requests_output": 2012, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-multistep:claude-opus-5-5:trial3", "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 5, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-13T04:48:07.599563+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 27.166, "t_checker_s": 0.379, "t_env_setup_s": 0.001, "task": "trig-omp-multistep", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "off", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s": 360, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "estimated", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens": 2028, "tokens_cache_read": 94484, "tokens_cache_write": 17627, "tokens_fresh": 2028, "tokens_input_uncached": 16, "tokens_main_cache_read": 94484, "tokens_main_cache_write": 17627, "tokens_main_calls": 7, "tokens_main_input_uncached": 16, "tokens_main_output": 2012, "tokens_output": 2012, "tokens_proxy_cache_read": 94484, "tokens_proxy_cache_write": 17627, "tokens_proxy_calls": 7, "tokens_proxy_input_uncached": 16, "tokens_proxy_output": 2012, "tokens_proxy_reasoning": null, "tokens_reasoning": 0, "trial": 3, "ts_iso": "2026-