w turns the amount into a string first, then converts it with `Decimal` and rounds half up to the nearest cent. Going through the string gives the shortest form of the float (`\"19.99\"`), so the binary error never gets into the calculation. Half-up rounding is also what `discounts.py` and `tax.py` already use. No other files changed.\n\n**How I tested:** there's no pytest on the system and pip won't install system-wide, so I made a throwaway venv at `/tmp/v` and ran `/tmp/v/bin/python -m pytest tests -q`. I couldn't run the suite against the old code because the directory isn't a git repo. The old behaviour (`19.99` \u2192 `1998`) is worked out from the code, not from a run I saw.\n\n**One open question:** a price with more than two decimals, like `1.005`, now rounds to the nearest cent instead of being cut off. If those should be rejected instead, `to_cents` needs to raise an error for them.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 0, "replies_ok": 6, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 79180, "requests_cache_write": 15782, "requests_cost_usd": 0.131082, "requests_count": 6, "requests_input_uncached": 14, "requests_output": 1814, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-multistep:claude-opus-5-5:trial5", "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 7, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-13T04:49:05.617188+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 23.698, "t_checker_s": 0.38, "t_env_setup_s": 0.001, "task": "trig-omp-multistep", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "off", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s": 360, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "estimated", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens": 1828, "tokens_cache_read": 79180, "tokens_cache_write": 15782, "tokens_fresh": 1828, "tokens_input_uncached": 14, "tokens_main_cache_read": 79180,